{"kind":"doc","route":"/guide/testing/extensible-architecture-graph","title":"Extensible architecture graph","blocks":[{"t":"heading","level":1,"id":"extensible-architecture-graph","children":[{"t":"text","text":"Extensible architecture graph"}]},{"t":"paragraph","children":[{"t":"text","text":"The Craft architecture graph is extensible by "},{"t":"strong","children":[{"t":"text","text":"TypeScript backend"}]},{"t":"text","text":", without"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"making the graph engine import that backend. Use this when an application has"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"server-side concepts that the built-in Craft graph cannot express: services,"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"layers, message brokers, data classifications, external outputs, or another"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"dependency-injection system."}]},{"t":"paragraph","children":[{"t":"text","text":"The extension has two separate parts:"}]},{"t":"list","ordered":false,"items":[[{"t":"paragraph","children":[{"t":"text","text":"a type extension, which gives rules typed "},{"t":"code","text":"kind"},{"t":"text","text":" details;"}]}],[{"t":"paragraph","children":[{"t":"text","text":"a runtime collector, which reads the TypeScript program and contributes"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"nodes, relations, diagnostics, and source proofs."}]}]]},{"t":"paragraph","children":[{"t":"text","text":"Importing the types never activates a collector."}]},{"t":"heading","level":2,"id":"_1-extend-the-vocabulary","children":[{"t":"text","text":"1. Extend the vocabulary"}]},{"t":"paragraph","children":[{"t":"text","text":"Add entries to the node and relation registries with module augmentation. The"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"augmentation must target the graph subpath:"}]},{"t":"code","lines":[{"tokens":[{"text":"import","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" "},{"text":"type","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" {","kind":"punctuation"}]},{"token